				267,
				5
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Add user extension retry + short-circuit Promise probes\n\nTwo fixes to the Output build pipeline:\n\n1. ExtensionScannerIPC: Mirror retry logic on user extensions scan path\n   The system extensions path had retry on empty response but user\n   extensions did not. Without it, an empty initial user-extensions\n   response silently passes 0 extensions through to viewsExtensionPoint\n   and ExtensionsRegistry, leaving every user extension contribution\n   (gitlens, clangd, commands, configuration, languages) unregistered.\n   Also switch to exponential backoff (100, 200, 400, 800, 1500ms) from\n   fixed 1000ms delays - Mountain's scan usually completes in ~500ms.\n\n2. TauriMainProcessService: Short-circuit Promise protocol probes\n   When VS Code resolves a channel-returned thenable, the JS runtime\n   accesses .then, .catch, .finally, constructor, valueOf, toString,\n   toJSON, @@iterator, @@asyncIterator on the proxy to determine if it's\n   a Promise. Each access became a channel call with the property name,\n   surfacing as \"Unknown IPC command: localPty:then\" on every workbench\n   wake. Returning undefined synchronously matches stock VS Code's\n   IChannel behaviour for unknown methods - the runtime sees a non-\n   thenable and stops probing. Saves ~15-25ms of round-trip per probe\n   and removes the noisiest IPC error in the dev log.\n\nRefs a28351b7240a5a722ebef039f3370ac90240818c (system ext retry)",
			"SHA": "2924f2ae8bb3b41fa32ae0fd965804a80d548dfa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T03:40:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				267,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Add retry logic to user extension scan path\n\nThe system extension scan path had retry logic but user extension scan\ndid not. Without retry on the user path, an empty initial response\nsilently passes 0 user extensions through to viewsExtensionPoint and\nExtensionsRegistry, which means every user-extension contribution\n(gitlens panes, clangd views, commands, configuration, languages)\nstays unregistered for the rest of the session.\n\nAdd the same retry logic to `extensions:scanUserExtensions` as already\nexists for `extensions:scanSystemExtensions`. Also switch to exponential\nbackoff (100, 200, 400, 800, 1500ms) instead of fixed 1000ms delays,\nsince Mountain's scan usually completes in ~500ms and the longer delays\nwere just padding boot time.\n\nUser extensions now load properly at boot even if Mountain's async disk\nscan hasn't completed yet.",
			"SHA": "a28351b7240a5a722ebef039f3370ac90240818c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T03:39:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
